  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SIDS Capacity Building Project: Safeguarding Heritage in the Pacific for Sustainable livelihood and Resilient Community through Community-Based Sustainable Tourism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A key objective of the project is to provide World Heritage stakeholders with the capacity and the tools to manage tourism efficiently, responsibly and sustainably based on the local context and needs. The project will also promote broad stakeholder engagement in the planning, developing, and managing of sustainable tourism that follows a destination approach to heritage conservation and focuses on empowering local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
